\f1\fs22 \'93Yes, darlin\'92 how can I help you?\'94 Elvine asked courteously.\
\'93Give me a small cordless stick blender or food processor. Now.\'94 Johnny demanded.\
\'93This is a bar and restaurant, sir, not an appliance store.\'94 Elvine retorted.\
\'93There will be one behind the bar. Go get it.\'94 He ordered, not even making eye-contact.\
\'93Yes, sir.\'94 She spun around and headed in the direction of the bar.\
\'93She took that pretty well. I was told they are not fond of the impolite.\'94 Sarah was most surprised. The way Cracker had explained it to her, you would find yourself in a very dangerous place if you are discourteous to the Elvi.\
\'93She knows how to take orders from her superiors.\'94 He smiled back. There was no way he would suck-up to a fucking beverage delivery system, his 
\f2\i dignitas 
\f1\i0 demanded otherwise.\
Elvine returned in double quick time, carrying a old glass blender. The glass \'91jug\'92 was in her right hand and the small base in her left. \
\'93I will just need the base. You know, the motor.\'94 Johnny said, sticking his hand out, again no eye contact.\
\'93You will get both.\'94 Elvine brought down the jug onto Johnny\'92s head, the glass shattering and slicing into his arrogant baldness. Blood raced out across his skull, then in-between a mash of interwoven fingers that failed to stem the flow. He collapsed and without a sound, he curled up in a ball on the sticky red carpet.
